        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(channels): core-owned durable ingress drain — one turn-adoption lifecycle, Telegram first",
        "body": "Closes #108656\n\nAI-assisted: yes. Implemented by grok-4.5 under Claude orchestration; every phase was structurally reviewed, adversarially re-reviewed per commit (Codex `gpt-5.6-sol` high), and independently validated before inclusion.\n\n> **Scope note:** per ClawSweeper's review recommendation (option 3) and maintainer decision, the WhatsApp migration was split out of this PR. Core + Telegram land here; WhatsApp follows in its own PR once the QA-lab live WhatsApp lane is re-linked (the shared broker's Baileys sessions are logged out). The split-out work — including fixes for two real WhatsApp adapter bugs found during validation (accept-path drain-idle await blocking multi-message upserts; dispatch-side re-normalization dropping messages whose LID mapping resolved only at receive time) — is preserved on branch `wa-durable-drain-followup` with the full WhatsApp suite green.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nTelegram was the only channel with a private transport-level turn-lifecycle layer (reply fence, ingress spool, per-transport claim/replay/watchdog loops duplicated across polling and webhook). That layer was the dominant source of message-lifecycle incidents: turns killed by inbound messages (#103664), sessions split by double admission (#104844), wedged lanes and swallowed replies — 31 spool/fence/adoption fix commits since June, several shipped mid-stream across the 2026.7.1 betas, with user reports still arriving on 2026.7.1. Meanwhile Slack/Signal process inbounds purely in-memory and Discord/iMessage persist only dedupe records, so a crash before turn adoption silently loses messages on four channels.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe reliability concepts were channel-agnostic but the implementation was Telegram-private and written twice. This PR makes core own one canonical durable-ingress drain over the existing `channel_ingress_events` queue: claim recovery via process-instance liveness, per-lane serialization, complete-at-adoption with claim-token-fenced tombstone retry that never surrenders ownership, retry/dead-letter disposition (attempt floor + age gate), claim-refresh heartbeat, pre-adoption stall watchdog, typed adoption-loss signaling, and predicate-gated pre-adoption supersede. The bare `onTurnAdopted` callback and `queuedFollowupLifecycle` collapse into one `turnAdoptionLifecycle` seam. Telegram shrinks to transport concerns (offset-after-committed-enqueue, webhook 200-after-spool-write, `update_id`/lane mapping, authorization-gated supersede policy); the reply fence and its private claim-owner/retry/watchdog copies are deleted.\n\nThe reliability invariants from `extensions/telegram/AGENTS.md` are now core contract tests (`src/channels/message/ingress-drain.test.ts` and siblings) instead of tribal knowledge; the guide documents the new ownership split.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe Telegram failure loop — nudging a busy bot kills/strands/splits its in-flight work, sessions degrade until `/new` — is structurally removed: channels no longer hold turn-interruption authority, and only authorized abort/commands (now including pairing-store, owner, group/topic-scoped allowlists, and own-bot command targeting) may supersede pre-adoption work. Message durability semantics (at-least-once, no replay of adopted turns, no silent loss on transient failures) are enforced in one place, and the other channels — WhatsApp first (follow-up branch ready), then Discord/Slack/Signal/iMessage — can adopt the same seam with a small adapter.\n\nLOC: total net −470 (+5,125/−5,595); Telegram prod −1,012, core drain +952 shared by six channels.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox full gate on the final stack: pairing-store auth guard, `pnpm tsgo` prod + test lanes, `pnpm plugin-sdk:surface:check`, `pnpm build`, and `pnpm test src/channels extensions/telegram extensions/whatsapp extensions/voice-call src/auto-reply src/gateway src/plugins src/plugin-sdk` — all green except two failures proven pre-existing on clean `origin/main` (`commands-plugins.install.test.ts` from #102197; `npm-install-security-scan.release.test.ts` google-meet dangerous-exec hit from #109413/#109466 — this diff touches neither).\n- Core drain contract tests: crash-window replay-exactly-once, complete-at-adoption, deferral holds claim, watchdog-through-deferral, supersede tombstones, dead-letter age gate, claim-token-fenced completion, two-drains-no-steal, heartbeat reclaim guillotine.\n- Telegram transport proof: offset-after-spool-ack, webhook redelivery on write failure, `update_id`/lane mapping, authorization-gated supersede incl. paired-DM/owner/topic-override/other-bot cases.\n- Structured per-commit review (Codex `gpt-5.6-sol`, high reasoning) across every phase; 29 accepted findings — including the four lifecycle races ClawSweeper confirmed — fixed with per-failure-window regression tests.\n- SDK seam narrowed per maintainer decision (see review thread): measured deltas +36 exports / +18 callable / +24 deprecated compat mirrors, documented inline in the surface-budget changelog.\n- Live behavior proof on real Telegram from this branch (see review thread): nudge-during-turn survives with both replies exactly-once (run M3TTZH), and a SIGKILL 400 ms after an inbound replays exactly-once after restart (run C9BTFU).\n",
